# CQ 19: Which data occur in a case, and of which kind?
#
# Clause 3.2 separates the data of a machine learning life cycle by the part
# they play: training data 3.2.17, validation data 3.2.19, evaluation and
# production data. They are disjoint in the pattern, since a set used for
# training and for evaluating at once would make the evaluation meaningless.
#
# Asked of the case rather than of the disjointness axioms. Reporting which
# kinds the pattern keeps apart would answer the same whichever model is
# loaded; reporting the data a case holds says what this system was built on.
#
# The direct kind is reported. The reasoner materialises the narrowest class,
# and naming Data alongside it would say nothing.
PREFIX iso:  <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
SELECT ?data ?kind ?usedBy
WHERE {
  ?data a ?kind . ?kind rdfs:subClassOf* iso:Data .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?data a ?narrower .
                      ?narrower rdfs:subClassOf+ ?kind ;
                                rdfs:subClassOf* iso:Data }
  OPTIONAL { ?usedBy iso:usesData ?data }
} ORDER BY ?kind ?data
